    "markingSchemeEn": "(a) 3 marks — one per section with its function, not merely named; the exposition earns full credit only if the second subject’s new key is mentioned.\n(b) 4 marks — the key relationship rather than the number of themes identified as central (2); the consequence for development and recapitulation if both were in the tonic (1); the recapitulation’s satisfaction located in the second subject remaining in the tonic (1).\n(c) 2 marks — at least two points at different levels (structural relations, the undervalued development, experience across time). \"A lot would be missed\" earns nothing.\nThe marks shown are a practice scale used on this platform, not an HKEAA mark allocation. The reference answer lists the required steps and criteria rather than a copyable model script. Compare your own work against it point by point; nothing here is machine-marked.",
